          "text": "Review complete. No supported finding within the scoped question:\n\n- The proposed repair in `src/platformdirs/unix.py` (`_site_data_dirs` / `_site_config_dirs`) splits on `os.pathsep` and keeps only entries where `os.path.isabs(p)` is true, which preserves absolute paths verbatim — including internal/trailing spaces, input order, and duplicates — while discarding empty and relative entries individually, and falls back to defaults only when no absolute entries remain.\n- The multipath property joins with `os.pathsep.join(dirs)` with no deduplication, so duplicates survive.\n- Grader cases `site-mixed` (`'/tmp/one/demo/2:/tmp/two/demo/2:/tmp/one/demo/2'`) and `creation-and-spaces` (`'/tmp/space name :/tmp/other'`) assert exactly what the requirement demands; no assertion contradicts it.\n\nSubmitted an empty findings list with limitations noted.",
